## Final answer of writer
I fixed the paging bug in `src/paginate.js`. When the item count was an exact multiple of the page size, the last page came out empty, so the last page's items were dropped. For example, `paginate(numbers(10), 5)` returned an empty last page instead of `[6, 7, 8, 9, 10]`.

The cause was the length calculation for the last page, which used `items.length % size`. That is 0 for an exact multiple. I removed it, and each page is now just `items.slice(start, start + size)`. `slice` stops at the end of the array, so a partial last page still holds the leftover items.

`npm test` now passes all 4 tests. Before the fix, 3 of 4 passed; the failing one was the existing exact-multiple test. I left no scratch files, and the only change in `git status` is `src/paginate.js`.

